solution_overview:
Let A = {2, 4, 6, 8, 10}, B = {3, 6, 9, 12}, and C = {1, 2, 3, 4, 5}.

**Part 1: Setup.**

Compute once: A ∩ B={6}; A B={2,3,4,6,8,9,10,12} (8 elements); C\A={1,3,5} (only removing ∪ 2,4, shared with A); B\C={6,9,12} (removing 3, the only shared element); A ∩ C={2,4} (only elements in both). Compare each statement below directly against these five reference values.

**Part 2: Check each claim.**

**1.** (TRUE) A ∩ B = {6}

**2.** (TRUE) A B has 8 elements ∪

**3.** (FALSE) C \ A = {1, 3}

**4.** (FALSE) B \ C = {3, 6, 9, 12}

**5.** (FALSE) A ∩ C = {2, 4, 6}

**Answer.** A=TRUE, B=TRUE, C=FALSE, D=FALSE, E=FALSE
